VERDICT: the quantitative body of Part 3b's firm statement —
   the roster must sit AT the Planck scale (O(1)·M_Pl, not near it
   logarithmically) with an O(1) spread across both sign pairs;
   a percent-class spread is excluded because str[km²lnm²] scales
   as the spread SQUARED (both linear terms die by the constraint),
   so small splittings drive the needed m far ABOVE M_Pl. The
   'spread O(M_Pl)' claim is now a computed locus, not a scaling
   argument. What this does NOT supply (unchanged): the emit
   mechanism and WHICH point on the locus the UV completion picks —
